:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240001} {:answer/id #uuid "ff20cf82-44db-5c30-a526-bae7c54563bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238471} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba6c1456-d2d2-5df1-9346-317b013edca8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240660}] :question/id #uuid "6e836e38-de2a-5e80-8414-a069ad09386c" :question/math-academy-id "q-105755" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=2 \\\\ 3{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=2$ and ${y}_{2}=-9.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241124 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d4b3937-d636-543e-b0d6-739f7a00e7f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 34\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238719} {:answer/id #uuid "59c3bb80-7b1c-535e-843c-7be8777981fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -34\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238826} {:answer/id #uuid "d6a16e65-a824-55dd-90aa-570d8ce9e4fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 24\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239931} {:answer/id #uuid "dbc1e9dc-6f28-50f2-90f2-765e57d990e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 36\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239972} {:answer/id #uuid "ec701eb0-1499-57d0-9f0b-83cacf08003b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -36\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 34\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238719} :answer-field/id #uuid "06e2738a-d273-5c9d-8b63-8b44a8f24c45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240338}] :question/id #uuid "d3a99bb0-e72d-5183-bc18-0817eb820005" :question/math-academy-id "q-105760" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -36\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -36\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=7 \\\\ -10{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=-36.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=7$ and ${y}_{2}=34.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 34\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244037 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "427af4b2-096b-5dbf-8f00-52882f2904b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 33\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241778} {:answer/id #uuid "565699cb-5aa4-56e7-8959-bd5585b64c79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241960} {:answer/id #uuid "9561d87e-a040-5eb9-9f47-8c4ea9835a94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242492} {:answer/id #uuid "b51413cc-3563-5af6-ac17-74e0247a8a5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242763} {:answer/id #uuid "cf0370c3-16bd-5ef9-95a0-be7a53155a4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 33\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241778} :answer-field/id #uuid "029bf18c-8249-5883-8d70-894701f6abe7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243440}] :question/id #uuid "d9df65e2-b577-593b-b89c-fc5d55ad0bf6" :question/math-academy-id "q-107171" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=5 \\\\ -7{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=-2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=5$ and ${y}_{2}=33.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 33\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244038 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56a516b1-0e57-5c35-a875-627c080854a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241961} {:answer/id #uuid "e9c6a2a3-37f8-522c-86b8-339400effadd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243247} {:answer/id #uuid "f5179545-dd33-5b3c-b9e0-1db909686ed7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243346} {:answer/id #uuid "fb403ca5-2870-5829-8af2-577957b21df2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answ