e eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{1}=2,$ and\n\n- the $2$nd column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2.$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404086 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7df3b7c7-8ab5-56e8-8b9c-3e3f6b261779" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=1,$ $b=7,$ and $c=-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404088} {:answer/id #uuid "bb986d69-47f8-539e-8e78-570956df6719" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=7,$ $b=1,$ and $c=-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404089} {:answer/id #uuid "5e7bfd3a-84c3-5bd7-86de-43e46a13b773" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=-2,$ $b=1,$ and $c=7$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404090} {:answer/id #uuid "72889b64-0d8f-5cf5-a078-304cd0270229" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=1,$ $b=-2,$ and $c=7$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404091} {:answer/id #uuid "d85b9e14-5285-547f-8225-bac68ffb2c7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=-2,$ $b=7,$ and $c=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404092}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=-2,$ $b=7,$ and $c=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404092} :answer-field/id #uuid "9085b031-ef66-5fae-9905-de9a5b2e5bed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404087}] :question/id #uuid "5e995591-79aa-5800-bd07-e99e51f5d9cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-80373" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $H$ for which ${\\lambda }_{1}=4$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2$ are eigenvalues, and\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nare the respective eigenvectors. What are the values of $a,b,c$ given that\n\n$$\nH=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -3 \\\\ b & c\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & a\\end{bmatrix}{\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -3 \\\\ b & c\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since the eigenvalues of the matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=4$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2,$ we construct the diagonal matrix $D$ by writing the eigenvalues in the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, to construct the matrix $P,$ we simply write the respective eigenvectors as columns: \n\n- the $1$st column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{1}=4,$ and\n\n- the $2$nd column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2.$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nH=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}{\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn conclusion, we get  $a=-2,$ $b=7,$ and $c=1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404093 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb0eb10f-8358-5f70-9dcf-5a12623a7ffa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$D=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}$ and \n$P=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404095} {:answer/id #uuid "1df643a8-80e1-5748-9179-fabd113dde47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$D=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}$ and \n$P=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404096} {:answer/id #uuid "0dd75f60-e366-51aa-9704-98e0a480bbc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$D=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}$ and \n$P=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404097} {:answer/id #uuid "fa9540b0-0bdb-50eb-99c1-9744cc3a5660" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$D=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$ and \n$P=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218